 "disposition": "clear",
 "priority": "low",
 "rationale": "A radiology order for P02741's active inpatient stay was sent to U0074's department (G9, G4); access came from a RAD workstation during U0074's scheduled shift amid routine multi-patient work (G10, G2, L13). The shared last name (G8) is noted, but a job-related purpose is shown, so the access clears; no escalation trigger applies."
}

{"what_happened": "Nurse U0047 accessed inpatient P01820's record 16 times between 15:16:54 and 15:36:38 on 2026-10-26 from MED2 workstations D0147 and D0269 (L1-L16, G9, G10), performing read, create, update, and query actions (G11).",
 "purpose_evidence": [
  {"claim": "U0047 is on the care team of encounter E006543, P01820's MED2 inpatient stay.", "sources": ["G7", "G4"]},
  {"claim": "That encounter was active at access time: inpatient in MED2 from 2026-10-16T16:08:15 to 2026-10-26T16:08:15, with all reviewed access falling 15:16-15:36 on the end date.", "sources": ["G4", "L1", "L16"]},
  {"claim": "U0047 is a full-time MED2 nurse scheduled in MED2 15:00-23:00 that day, and both devices used are MED2 workstations.", "sources": ["G1", "G2", "G9", "G10"]},
  {"claim": "The session mixed reads with creates (A0137, A0218, A0282), an update (A0037), and queries (A0357, A0374), including long documentation-style entries (e.g., L15, 300s).", "sources": ["G11", "L12", "L13", "L15", "L16"]},
  {"claim": "Other users accessed P01820 the same day across several devices (L47-L76), and U0047 worked many other patients the same shift (L17-L46), consistent with an active unit assignment.", "sources": ["L47", "L61", "L76", "L17", "L34"]}
 ],
 "risk_indicators": [
  {"claim": "The accessed record carries a stigmatizing diagnosis, dependent drug abuse (disorder), a sensitive category that merits audit attention.", "sources": ["G4"]},
  {"claim": "The graph's 'co-worker' flags link the pair only through department MED2, the encounter's own department; no fact shows a family, friend, or other personal relationship.", "sources": ["G5", "G6", "G8"]}
 ],
 "missing_information": [
  "Effective dates of U0047's care-team assignment (G7 shows the link but no date range), to confirm it was active on 2026-10-26.",
  "Optionally, the unit's patient assignment for that shift, if policy requires documented assignment beyond the care-team link."
 ],
 "disposition": "clear",
 "priority": "low",
 "rationale": "Care-team link (G7), active MED2 encounter (G4), and on-shift, on-unit access (G2, G9, G10) show job-related purpose. 'Co-worker' edges (G5, G6) trace only to shared department MED2 (G8), not a personal tie. Sensitive diagnosis (G4) alone does not overcome the purpose shown. Clear, low."
}

{"what_happened": "Billing coder U0265 opened patient P01940's record three times in ~17 seconds at 11:39 on 2026-10-27 — one query (A0374) and two reads (A0165, A0335) — from D0390, a BILL workstation, during their scheduled shift (L1, L2, L3, G9, G2, G10). The same user accessed many other patients across devices that same day (L4, L15, L23, L26, L30, L33).",
 "purpose_evidence": [
   {"claim": "U0265 is a full-time coder in the Billing department on an office shift", "sources": ["G1"]},
   {"claim": "The reviewed access fell inside U0265's 08:00-17:00 scheduled shift and occurred on a BILL-department workstation", "sources": ["L1", "L2", "L3", "G2", "G9"]},
   {"claim": "P01940 had five encounters in the two weeks before the access (ORTH 10-15 and 10-21 with fracture diagnoses, ED 10-21 and 10-22, PCP 10-23), the kind of activity that plausibly requires coding", "sources": ["G3", "G4", "G5", "G6", "G7"]},
   {"claim": "U0265 accessed dozens of other patients within the same 12-hour window across devices D0129, D0256, and D0390", "sources": ["L4", "L15", "L23", "L26", "L30", "L33"]}
 ],
 "risk_indicators": [
   {"claim": "No personal connection between U0265 and P01940 is recorded in the identity graph, so no relationship-based concern appears", "sources": ["G8"]},
   {"claim": "No fact documents a coding assignment, worklist entry, or open billing task linking U0265 to P01940's encounters, so a job-related purpose is not shown by the facts alone", "sources": ["L1", "L2", "L3", "G1", "G3", "G4", "G5", "G6", "G7"]}
 ],
 "missing_information": [
   "Whether P01940's recent encounters (G3-G7) were assigned to U0265's coding worklist or an open billing account on 2026-10-27",
   "Whether U0265's normal coding workflow includes a query (A0374) followed by short reads on assigned charts (G10)",
   "Whether department policy permits coder access to any patient record or restricts it to assigned accounts"
 ],
 "disposition": "verify",
 "priority": "low",
 "rationale": "Facts show a billing coder accessing during shift on a BILL workstation, with no recorded personal tie to the patient and a same-day multi-patient pattern; but no fact documents a coding assignment for P01940, and none shows a concern on its own. Ask the supervisor to confirm the chart was on U0265's worklist."
}

